<article class="guide-article bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="Wi-Fi coverage or internet service: what should you record?">
  <div class="guide-reading mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The connection feels fine at the kitchen table but unreliable in the study. Is the internet plan too slow, or is the difficulty getting a useful connection to that room? Before changing a plan or buying equipment, make a small map of the experience.</p>
{% include "components/guide-start.njk" %}
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Start with a room map</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Draw your home's rooms on paper. Mark the router's location and the places where you normally work, stream or make calls. You do not need measurements or a professional floor plan. Use labels such as “study desk” rather than an address if you share the notes.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Beside each location, record one ordinary task and what happened. Keep the device and task the same for the first comparison. This is a record of your experience, not a signal survey.</p>
